-- title:
--   Points over the closed point are closed or branch generic points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a term $\mathfrak X$ of the structure `DRModelPackage p`, which bundles the properness, flatness, integrality and normality of the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ together with its rational and geometric curve models, two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$, a smooth locus and further data. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $y$ be a point of the scheme $\mathfrak X_O$ obtained as the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, and assume that the second projection sends $y$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$. The conclusion is a threefold disjunction: either the singleton $\{y\}$ is closed in $\mathfrak X_O$, or $y$ is the image of the generic point of $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{ratModel}\ k).C$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\ k$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` (the map from the base change along $k$ to the base change along $O$ induced by $\mathrm{to}\kappa$), or $y$ is the image of that generic point under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\ k$ followed by the same base-change map.
--
--   This is the point-set description of the fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ over the closed point of a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: apart from the generic points of the two branches, every point of that fibre is closed in the total space. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_integers_and_mem_integers_of_stalk_of_specializes).
